## 1. Introduction

This rule defines visual patterns and conventions for **UU5 client-side component diagrams** and **uuApp topology diagrams**. It is NOT a general rule for all uuBml diagram types.

### 1.1 Scope

This rule covers:

- **UU5 Component Diagrams** — Visual representations of client-side component hierarchies (routes, visual components, non-visual components, hooks, methods, uuCommands)
- **uuApp Topology Diagrams** — Application structure showing uuApp, uuSubApps, data stores, and libraries

This rule does NOT cover:
- General uuBml diagrams (use cases, activity diagrams, etc.)
- Server-side command flow diagrams
- Business process diagrams
- Other specialized uuBml diagram types

### 1.2 Key Characteristics

- Visual conventions follow the official uuBml Cheatsheet and uuApp Model conventions
- Diagrams communicate one clear idea with consistent styling
- Elements use proper importance levels reflecting their semantic role
- Connectors use appropriate routing (diagonal or orthogonal) based on layout
- Labels and naming follow established patterns for UU5 components

Use this rule together with the `/bml-diagram` skill (which handles the technical generation).

### 1.3 When to Apply

Apply this rule when:
- Creating component diagrams for UU5 routes and visual components
- Creating uuApp topology diagrams showing application structure
- Documenting client-side component hierarchies
- Reviewing or validating existing UU5 component diagrams

## 2. Core Principles

These five principles are from the official uuBml Cheatsheet.

### 2.1 One Key Idea Per Diagram

- Each diagram communicates **one clear idea**
- For complex topics, use **separate diagrams for details**, then a summary diagram combining them

### 2.2 Use Standard uuBml Formats

- Do NOT change established icon styles and colors
- Use icons **only for their intended purpose**
- If no matching icon exists, use "Missing Icon" and note it
- Use association arrows (1:1, aggregation 1:n, etc.) **exactly in their standard meanings**

### 2.3 Style Consistency

- A particular icon must have **only one meaning** within the diagram
- Use **different arrow formats** for different relationship types
- Name objects of the same type with **the same word classes** (e.g., activities as infinitives)
- Attach arrows to **the same socket positions** on icons (not one higher and another lower)

### 2.4 Simplicity and Readability

- Read direction: **left to right, top to bottom**
- Remove any icon or label that doesn't need to be there
- **Generate HIGH-LEVEL diagrams by default** — show only the most important components, hooks, and commands
- Do NOT include every import, helper function, or internal state variable as a separate icon
- Group HOC chains into a single parent "Route" concept with dashed lines

### 2.5 Alignment and Attachment

- **Always attach** arrows, callouts, and annotations to the icons they reference
- Do NOT cross or overlap arrows with other objects
- Arrows should **point to the center** of an icon when possible
- **Align icons with the grid** (between thicker grid lines)
- Keep **uniform spacing** between icons
- Do NOT overlap icon labels

## 3. Icon Stencil Reference

### 3.1 Mandatory Icon Types for UU5 Component Diagrams

These are the **exact stencil and icon code combinations** to use. Do NOT use incorrect stencils. Pass them via `type: { stencil: '...', icon: '...' }` in the generator.

| Element | Stencil | Icon Code | Generator Usage |
|---|---|---|---|
| **User visual entrypoint (uu5Uve)** | `uuappmodelkit` | `uu5Uve` | `type: { stencil: 'uuappmodelkit', icon: 'uu5Uve' }` |
| **Route (uu5Route)** | `uu5` | `route` | `type: { stencil: 'uu5', icon: 'route' }` |
| **Visual component** | `uu5` | `visualComponent` | `type: { stencil: 'uu5', icon: 'visualComponent' }` |
| **Non-visual component** | `uu5` | `nonVisualComponent` | `type: { stencil: 'uu5', icon: 'nonVisualComponent' }` |
| **General component** | `uuappcommon` | `contentComponent` | `type: { stencil: 'uuappcommon', icon: 'contentComponent' }` |
| **Higher-order component (HoC)** | `uu5` | `higherOrderComponent` | `type: { stencil: 'uu5', icon: 'higherOrderComponent' }` |
| **uuCommand** | `uuappcommon` | `command` | `type: { stencil: 'uuappcommon', icon: 'command' }` |
| **Method / Handler** | `uuappcommon` | `method` | `type: { stencil: 'uuappcommon', icon: 'method' }` |
| **Hook (uu5Hook)** | `uuappmodelkit` | `uu5Hook` | `type: { stencil: 'uuappmodelkit', icon: 'uu5Hook' }` |
| **Context** | `uuappmodelkit` | `uu5Context` | `type: { stencil: 'uuappmodelkit', icon: 'uu5Context' }` |
| **Context Provider** | `uu5` | `contextProvider` | `type: { stencil: 'uu5', icon: 'contextProvider' }` |
| **Context Consumer** | `uu5` | `contextConsumer` | `type: { stencil: 'uu5', icon: 'contextConsumer' }` |

### 3.2 When to Use Each Icon

**Component Types:**
- **uu5Uve (User Visual Entrypoint)** — Base of uuApp Human Interface, designed as SPA. One application can have multiple uu5Uves.
- **Route (uu5Route)** — Individually addressable parts of SPA with its own URL. Encapsulates business logic.
- **Visual component** — Dumb components responsible for visualizing content.
- **Non-visual component** — Smart components that obtain data and pass it to visual components via props. Can encapsulate business logic.
- **General component** — Use when unknown whether the component will be visual or non-visual.
- **Higher-order component (HoC)** — Function that receives a component and returns a new enhanced component without modifying the original.

**Hooks and Context:**
- **uu5Hook** — Reusable component parts with logic, based on React Hooks.
- **Context** — Used for passing data through component hierarchy without prop drilling (Provider/Consumer pattern).
- **Context Provider** — Component that allows consuming components to subscribe to context changes.
- **Context Consumer** — Component that subscribes to context changes. Note: For each context a hook is automatically generated - prefer using the hook icon in diagrams.

**API and Methods:**
- **uuCommand** — Non-visual subapplication interface (API layer), represents a particular use case. Icon is always yellow (`highest` importance).
- **Method / Handler** — Used to indicate interface methods, component methods in interface, or handlers passed via context/props.

### 3.3 uuCommand Callout Rules

- **Always look for uuCmd calls** in the component's providers and hooks. Trace from hooks → providers → `Calls.*` to find the actual server commands.
- uuCommand icons are **always `highest` importance** (yellow) — no exceptions.
- Place uuCommand icons to the **right** of the hook/method that calls them.
- Connect hook → uuCommand with horizontal `association1`, solid line.
- Label uuCommand icons with the actual command path (e.g., `entityItem/get`, `entityItem/update`).

## 4. Importance Levels

Each importance level maps to a specific visual color. The meaning depends on diagram context.

### 4.1 Color Mapping

| Importance | Color | General Meaning | Component Diagram Meaning |
|---|---|---|---|
| `objective` | Orange/amber | The **main subject** of the diagram | The described component |
| `highest` | Yellow | Primary highlighted elements | **uuCommand** (always yellow) |
| `high` | Blue | Important supporting elements | Component with **its own detail page** |
| `normal` | Gray | Standard elements | Common component from another library |
| `low` | Light gray | Background/future elements | Components for later implementation |

### 4.2 Importance Rules

- The **focal element** of the diagram always gets `objective`
- **uuCommand icons are ALWAYS `highest`** (yellow) — this is mandatory, no exceptions
- Parent/container components in component diagrams use `normal` or `low`
- Components described in detail elsewhere use `high`
- External library components use `normal` (library identified by namespace, e.g., `Uu5Tiles.List`)

## 5. Connector Patterns

### 5.1 Parent-Child Connectors (Component Hierarchies)

In component hierarchy diagrams, connectors are **straight diagonal lines** from the child's **top-center** to the parent's **bottom-center** socket. This is the standard pattern in official uuBml diagrams:

```json
"middlePointList": []
```

When `middlePointList` is empty and the two plug positions have different X and Y coordinates, the result is a **diagonal line**. Children at different horizontal positions naturally create diagonal lines to the parent above.

**Key rules for hierarchy connectors:**
- Child icon's **top-center socket** connects to parent's **bottom-center socket** (or nearby socket when multiple children share the same parent)
- Icons on the **same Y position** are at the **same hierarchical level**
- The parent is always **above** (lower Y value) the children
- Lines are straight with no breakpoints — diagonal is expected and correct

**When to use diagonal connectors:**
- Parent-child relationships where children are offset horizontally from the parent
- Hub-and-spoke layouts (e.g., uuSubApps radiating from uuApp)
- Any connection where a direct line is clean and doesn't cross other elements

**In the generator**, use `diagonal: true` option:
```js
builder.connect(childIcon, parentIcon, { diagonal: true, relationType: 'association1' });
```

### 5.2 Orthogonal Connectors (Right-Angle Lines)

For situations requiring orthogonal routing, use `middlePointList` with breakpoints:

- **L-shaped**: One breakpoint creates a 90-degree turn
- **S-shaped**: Two breakpoints create two 90-degree turns

**When to use orthogonal connectors:**
- Horizontal connections between aligned elements (same Y), e.g., Component → uuCommand
- Vertical connections between perfectly stacked elements (same X)
- Complex routing where diagonal lines would cross other elements

### 5.3 Connector Direction Convention

The `startPoint` (with `pointer: "one"`) is on the **child/owned element**. The `endPoint` (with `pointer: "association"`) is on the **parent/owner**:

- Data Store → uuSubApp (store belongs to SubApp)
- uuSubApp → uuApp (SubApp belongs to App)
- Child Component → Parent Component

### 5.4 Relation Types

| Relation Type | Start Pointer | End Pointer | When to Use |
|---|---|---|---|
| `association1` | `"one"` | `"association"` | 1:1 composition/containment (most common) |
| `associationN` | `null` | `"association"` | 1:N composition (iteration pattern) |
| `aggregation1` | `null` | `"aggregation"` | Has-a relationship (hollow diamond) |
| `aggregationN` | `null` | `"aggregation"` | Object is part of another (in lists/maps) |
| `composition1` | `null` | `"composition"` | Strong ownership (filled diamond) |
| `compositionN` | `null` | `"composition"` | Composition with N multiplicity |
| `inheritance` | `null` | `"inheritance"` | Extends/implements (triangle) |
| `general` | `null` | `"general"` | Invocation/reference (method → uuCmd) |

**Pointer Types (for custom configurations):**
| Pointer Value | Visual | Description |
|---|---|---|
| `null` | (none) | No pointer/arrow |
| `"general"` | → | Simple arrow head |
| `"one"` | 1 | Multiplicity indicator |
| `"association"` | ◇ | Hollow diamond (association) |
| `"aggregation"` | ◇ | Hollow diamond (aggregation) |
| `"composition"` | ◆ | Filled diamond (composition) |
| `"inheritance"` | △ | Triangle (inheritance) |

### 5.5 Line Styles

| Style | Meaning |
|---|---|
| `solid` | Direct relationship — component is directly nested in parent |
| `dashed` | **Intermediate components omitted** — "there are more components between, but they're not important for this diagram" |
| `dotted` | Optional/weak dependency (e.g., dependency on external uuSubApp) |

### 5.6 Connection Presets (Generator Helper Methods)

The generator library provides **preset-based helper methods** for common connection patterns. Use these instead of manually specifying `relationType`, `lineStyle`, and pointer values:

| Preset / Method | Visual | relationType | lineStyle | When to Use |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| `connect(from, to)` | → | `general` | `solid` | Standard arrow (default) |
| `connectAssociation(from, to)` | ◇—1 | `association1` | `solid` | Parent-child containment |
| `connectSkip(from, to)` | ◇- -1 | `association1` | `dashed` | Indirect relationship (HOCs omitted) |
| `connectAggregation(from, to)` | ◇ | `aggregation1` | `solid` | Has-a relationship |
| `connectComposition(from, to)` | ◆ | `composition1` | `solid` | Strong ownership |
| `connectInheritance(from, to)` | △ | `inheritance` | `solid` | Extends/implements |
| `connectLine(from, to)` | ── | `general` | `solid` | Plain line (no arrows) |

**Using presets with `connect()`:**
```javascript
// Using preset parameter
builder.connect(child, parent, { preset: 'association' });
builder.connect(child, parent, { preset: 'skip' });  // dashed association

// Using helper methods (recommended)
builder.connectAssociation(child, parent);
builder.connectSkip(child, parent);  // dashed association for omitted HOCs
```

**MANDATORY for component diagrams:**
- Use `connectAssociation()` for direct parent-child relationships
- Use `connectSkip()` when intermediate components (HOCs) are omitted
- Use `connect()` (default arrow) for method → uuCmd references

### 5.7 Annotation Bubbles (Callouts)

Annotations are **speech bubble callouts** with pointers that explain elements in the diagram. Use them for:
- Explaining what a connection or icon represents
- Adding context about component behavior
- Describing relationship semantics

**Generator usage:**
```javascript
// Annotation pointing to an icon
builder.addAnnotation({
    position: { x: 700, y: 448 },
    size: { width: 176, height: 72 },
    text: '<uu5string/><div style="<uu5json />{\\\"lineHeight\\\":\\\"13px\\\"}">Explanation text here.</div>',
    targetIcon: commandIcon,
    pointerSide: 'left'  // 'top', 'right', 'bottom', 'left'
});

// Floating annotation (no pointer) for titles/notes
builder.addFloatingAnnotation({
    position: { x: 100, y: 50 },
    size: { width: 200, height: 48 },
    text: '<uu5string/><div>Diagram Title</div>'
});
```

**Pointer side values:**
| Side | orderInPolygon | Description |
|---|---|---|
| `top` | 1 | Pointer exits from top edge |
| `right` | 2 | Pointer exits from right edge |
| `bottom` | 3 | Pointer exits from bottom edge |
| `left` | 4 | Pointer exits from left edge |

**Annotation rules:**
- Use `lineHeight: "13px"` for compact text
- Typical sizes: width 176-288px, height 48-112px
- Place annotations in **open spaces** near the elements they describe
- Point to the **center of the icon** when possible

## 6. Layout Patterns

### 6.1 uuApp Topology Diagram

Hub-and-spoke layout:

```
                    ┌─ uuSubApp A ─── primary ─── binary
                   ╱
    uuApp ────────
                   ╲
                    └─ uuSubApp B ─── primary
       │
       ├── uuAppServerLibrary
       └── uu5ComponentLibrary
```

| Element | Position | Importance |
|---|---|---|
| uuApp | Center-left as hub | `objective` |
| uuSubApps | Upper-right, stacked vertically (~128px) | `highest` |
| Data stores | Extend horizontally right from SubApps | `high` |
| Libraries | Extend downward from uuApp | `highest` |
| Block | Wraps everything, label "Application structure" at top | `normal` |

**Connections:** Diagonal from SubApps/Libraries to uuApp; horizontal from data stores to SubApps.

### 6.2 Client-Side Component Diagram

Hierarchical top-down layout where **Y position = hierarchy level**:

```
    Parent Component (normal/low, gray)
          │                                  ← vertical line (same X)
    Main Component (objective, orange)
        ╱ │ ╲                                ← diagonal lines to children
    Child A  Child B  Child C                   (all on same Y = same level)
       │                                     ← vertical/diagonal to deeper children
    Method ──→ uuCmd (highest, yellow)       ← horizontal "general" connector
```

**Hierarchy is reflected by Y position:**
- Icons on the **same Y coordinate** are at the **same hierarchical level**
- Parent icons are **above** (lower Y) their children
- Children spread **horizontally** at the next Y level

**Connector routing in hierarchies:**
- Parent-to-child: straight lines from parent's **bottom-center** to child's **top-center** (diagonal when horizontally offset)
- Same-level references: horizontal connectors (Component → uuCommand via `general` relation)
- Use `diagonal: true` in the generator for hierarchy connectors

| Level | Y Position | Elements |
|---|---|---|
| Top | ~128 | Parent route / User visual entrypoint (`normal`, gray) — `uuappmodelkit`/`uu5Uve` |
| Main | ~320 | Main component (`objective`, orange) — `uu5`/`route` |
| Wrapper | ~448 | Non-visual wrappers (`high`, blue) — `uu5`/`nonVisualComponent` |
| Children | ~576 | Child visual components (various importances) — `uu5`/`visualComponent` |
| Right of main | ~320 | Hooks using `uuappmodelkit`/`uu5Hook` |
| Right of wrapper | ~448, ~576 | Context providers using `uu5`/`contextProvider` |
| Far right | ~256, ~384, ~448 | uuCmd callouts (`highest`, yellow) — `uuappcommon`/`command` |

**Example — Component with parent, hooks, callouts, and children:**
```
    Route (uuappmodelkit/uu5Uve, normal, y=128)
          │ (dashed = HOCs omitted)
    MainComponent (uu5/route, objective, y=320) ── useHook (uuappmodelkit/uu5Hook) ── cmd/get (uuappcommon/command, highest)
          │                                                                        ── cmd/update (uuappcommon/command, highest)
    ContentContainer (uu5/nonVisualComponent, high, y=448) ── Entity.Provider (uu5/contextProvider) ── cmd/get (highest)
        ╱           ╲
  ChildA (uu5/visualComponent, high)    ChildB (uu5/visualComponent, normal)     (all at y=576)
```

- Route→MainComponent: `association1`, **dashed**, `diagonal: true`
- MainComponent→useHook: `association1`, solid (horizontal)
- useHook→cmd/get, cmd/update: `association1`, solid (horizontal)
- MainComponent→ContentContainer: `association1`, solid, `diagonal: true`
- ContentContainer→[ChildA, ChildB]: `MultiConnector`, `inverted: true`, `direction: 'vertical'`
- ContentContainer→Entity.Provider: `association1`, solid (horizontal)

### 6.3 Three Composition Patterns (Client-Side)

| Pattern | Connector Type | Description |
|---|---|---|
| **Sequence** | `association1`, solid | Children always displayed in specific order |
| **Selection** | `MultiConnector` with `inverted: true` | Only one child conditionally displayed |
| **Iteration** | `associationN` | Same component displayed multiple times |

**Warning:** Do NOT combine MultiConnector (selection) with the `r` label — the multitree arrow already indicates conditional rendering.

### 6.4 General Positioning Rules

- Grid alignment: all positions on **8px grid** (coordinates divisible by 8)
- Standard icon spacing: **128px** between hierarchy levels (vertical Y gap)
- Horizontal spacing between siblings: **256px** minimum for wide layout, **128px** minimum for compact
- Canvas width: **1600px** minimum for component diagrams (to accommodate callouts on the right)
- Block padding from canvas edge: **40px**
- Read flow: **left → right, top → bottom**
- Component hierarchy spans the **left-center area**, hooks extend to the **right**, uuCmd callouts extend to the **far right**

## 7. Icon Labels

Labels appear as small indicators on icon corners.

| Label Code | Symbol | Meaning |
|---|---|---|
| `uujson` / `{}` | `{}` | Object represents a single scheme in an object store |
| `n` | N | Multi-workspace uuSubApp (N app workspaces) |
| `one` | 1 | Single-workspace uuSubApp (1 app workspace) |
| `r` | R | Rendered conditionally |
| `d` | D | Disabled conditionally |
| `h` | H | Hidden conditionally |
| `lock` | Lock | Combination of conditions (R+D) |
| `l` | L | Part of a **list** (aggregation) |
| `m` | M | Part of a **map** (aggregation) |

### 7.1 Label Rules

- uuSubApps **must** be labeled with `one` or `n` to indicate workspace multiplicity
- Objects representing a scheme in object store **must** have `{}` label
- Aggregated objects that are NOT standalone schemes get **no label** (or `l`/`m`)
- Do NOT combine `r` label with MultiConnector selection pattern

## 8. Naming Conventions

### 8.1 Text Labels

| Entity | Convention | Example |
|---|---|---|
| uuApp | Simple name | `uuApp` |
| uuSubApp | lowerCamelCase | `main`, `uuSubApp A` |
| Data stores | Name + stereotype on second line | `primary\n<<uuAppObjectStore>>` |
| Routes | Route name + stereotype | `Route name\n<<uu5Route>>` |
| Components (same module) | Just name | `JokeListView` |
| Components (same lib, different module) | Module.Name | `Joke.ListView` |
| Components (different lib) | Full tag | `Uu5Tiles.List` |
| Non-separate components | `//` prefix comment | `Component\n// render` |

### 8.2 Text Width

| Width | Use For |
|---|---|
| `64` | Short labels (uuApp) |
| `128` | Medium labels (uuSubApps, components) |
| `192` | Long labels with stereotypes (data stores, routes) |

### 8.3 Annotation Text

- Use `lineHeight: "13px"` for compact display
- Typical sizes: width 176-288px, height 48-112px
- Place annotations in **open spaces** near the elements they describe

## 9. Best Practices

- **High-level by default** — generate high-level diagrams showing only the key components, hooks, and commands. Do NOT add every import or helper.
- **Wide layout** — use canvas width **1600px or wider** to give elements room. Default spacing between siblings should be **256px** horizontally.
- **Always include callouts (uuCmd)** — trace hooks → providers → `Calls.*` to find all server commands and add them to the diagram as yellow (`highest`) command icons.
- **One idea per diagram** — split complex topics into multiple diagrams.
- **Focal element is `objective`** — always highlight the main subject.
- **uuCommand is always yellow** — no exceptions, always `highest`.
- **Correct icon stencils** — use the exact stencil/icon combinations from Section 3. Do NOT use generic fallbacks.
- **Hierarchy = Y position** — icons at the same Y are at the same hierarchical level.
- **Use diagonal lines for hierarchies** — parent-child connectors are straight diagonal lines (top-center of child to bottom-center of parent), use `diagonal: true` in the generator.
- **Use orthogonal lines for same-level references** — horizontal/vertical for Component→uuCommand or similar.
- **Label uuSubApps** — always indicate `one` or `n` for workspace multiplicity.
- **Use dashed lines** — when intermediate components (HOCs) are omitted for clarity.
- **Use connection helper methods** — prefer `connectAssociation()`, `connectSkip()`, etc. over manual `connect()` with options.
- **Use annotations for context** — add `addAnnotation()` callouts to explain hooks, commands, or complex relationships.
- **Consistent socket positions** — connectors attach at top-center (child) and bottom-center (parent).
- **Grid alignment** — all positions on 8px grid for clean rendering.
- **Z-order** — Blocks (bottom) → Icons → Annotations → Connectors (top).

### 9.1 Component Analysis Checklist

When asked to generate a UU5 component diagram, follow this analysis order:

1. **Identify the main component** — the `createVisualComponent` call → this becomes the `objective` icon using `uu5` / `route`.
2. **Identify the parent** — HOC chain or route wrapper → abstract as single `uuappmodelkit` / `uu5Uve` icon with dashed line.
3. **Identify HOC wrappers** — `withRoute`, `withEditModal`, etc. → `uu5` / `higherOrderComponent` (or omit and use dashed line).
4. **Identify key hooks** — `useEntityItem`, `useEntityDefinition`, `useBusinessBrick`, etc. → `uuappmodelkit` / `uu5Hook`.
5. **Identify context usage** — Provider/Consumer patterns → `uuappmodelkit` / `uu5Context` for context, `uu5` / `contextProvider` for providers.
6. **Trace uuCmd calls** — follow hooks → providers → `Calls.*` methods to find actual server commands (e.g., `entityItem/get`, `entityItem/update`) → `uuappcommon` / `command` with `highest` importance.
7. **Identify child visual components** — direct children rendered in JSX → `uu5` / `visualComponent`.
8. **Identify non-visual wrappers** — `ContentContainer`, `DataStateResolver`, etc. → `uu5` / `nonVisualComponent`.
9. **Identify general components** — when visual/non-visual nature is unknown → `uuappcommon` / `contentComponent`.
10. **Identify conditional rendering** — if/else or switch rendering multiple children → use `MultiConnector` with `inverted: true`.

## 10. Reference Template

### 10.1 Generator Script Template

Use this template when generating UU5 component diagrams:

```js
const { DiagramBuilder } = require('/Users/jilek/.claude/skills/bml-diagram/lib/bml-generator');
const fs = require('fs');

// Wide canvas for readable layout
const builder = new DiagramBuilder({ width: 1600, height: 900 });

// === ROW 1: Parent route (y=128) ===
const parentRoute = builder.addIcon({
  type: { stencil: 'uuappmodelkit', icon: 'uu5Uve' },
  position: { x: 640, y: 128 },
  text: 'Route',
  textWidth: 128,
  importance: 'normal'
});

// === ROW 2: Main component (y=320, objective = orange) ===
const mainComponent = builder.addIcon({
  type: { stencil: 'uu5', icon: 'route' },
  position: { x: 640, y: 320 },
  text: 'ComponentName',
  textWidth: 192,
  importance: 'objective'
});

// === Hooks on the right of main component ===
const hook1 = builder.addIcon({
  type: { stencil: 'uuappmodelkit', icon: 'uu5Hook' },
  position: { x: 960, y: 320 },
  text: 'useHookName',
  textWidth: 128,
  importance: 'normal'
});

// === uuCmd callouts (always highest = yellow) ===
const cmd1 = builder.addIcon({
  type: { stencil: 'uuappcommon', icon: 'command' },
  position: { x: 1216, y: 256 },
  text: 'entity/get',
  textWidth: 128,
  importance: 'highest'
});

const cmd2 = builder.addIcon({
  type: { stencil: 'uuappcommon', icon: 'command' },
  position: { x: 1216, y: 384 },
  text: 'entity/update',
  textWidth: 144,
  importance: 'highest'
});

// === ROW 3: Non-visual wrapper (y=448) ===
const contentWrapper = builder.addIcon({
  type: { stencil: 'uu5', icon: 'nonVisualComponent' },
  position: { x: 640, y: 448 },
  text: 'ContentContainer',
  textWidth: 192,
  importance: 'high'
});

// === ROW 4: Child visual components (y=576) ===
const childA = builder.addIcon({
  type: { stencil: 'uu5', icon: 'visualComponent' },
  position: { x: 448, y: 576 },
  text: 'ChildComponentA',
  textWidth: 192,
  importance: 'high'
});

const childB = builder.addIcon({
  type: { stencil: 'uu5', icon: 'visualComponent' },
  position: { x: 832, y: 576 },
  text: 'ChildComponentB',
  textWidth: 128,
  importance: 'normal'
});

// === Context provider example ===
const contextProvider = builder.addIcon({
  type: { stencil: 'uu5', icon: 'contextProvider' },
  position: { x: 1088, y: 448 },
  text: 'Entity.Provider',
  textWidth: 160,
  importance: 'normal'
});

// === CONNECTIONS ===

// Parent to main (dashed = HOCs omitted) - use connectSkip helper
builder.connectSkip(mainComponent, parentRoute, { diagonal: true });

// Main to hook (horizontal) - use connectAssociation helper
builder.connectAssociation(hook1, mainComponent);

// Hook to commands (horizontal) - use connectAssociation helper
builder.connectAssociation(cmd1, hook1);
builder.connectAssociation(cmd2, hook1);

// Main to content wrapper (vertical/diagonal)
builder.connectAssociation(contentWrapper, mainComponent, { diagonal: true });

// Content wrapper to children (selection = MultiConnector)
builder.connectMultiAssociation(contentWrapper, [childA, childB], {
  inverted: true, direction: 'vertical'
});

// Context provider to wrapper (horizontal)
builder.connectAssociation(contextProvider, contentWrapper);

// === ANNOTATIONS (example) ===

// Add a callout explaining the hook's purpose
builder.addAnnotation({
  position: { x: 1100, y: 256 },
  size: { width: 176, height: 64 },
  text: '<uu5string/><div style="<uu5json />{\\\"lineHeight\\\":\\\"13px\\\"}">Fetches entity data and manages update state</div>',
  targetIcon: hook1,
  pointerSide: 'left'
});

// === SAVE ===
const uu5 = builder.toUu5String();
fs.writeFileSync('/tmp/diagram_output.txt', uu5);
console.log('Diagram saved to /tmp/diagram_output.txt');
console.log('Size:', uu5.length, 'bytes');
```

